  "reviewFindings": [
    "Independent read-only review found no blocker and made no production edit.",
    "The turn deadline is based on the execution budget start, including memory preparation time; cancellation/hard deadline win same-boundary settlement.",
    "Only read-only preparation is abandoned. The real provider retains its single in-flight slot until settlement; late resolve does not touch turn state and late reject remains observed.",
    "Production retrieval uses recordFeedback:false. Only admitted memory gets retrieved/injected accounting, bound to the active turnId. Late memory neither writes usefulness/tokenROI nor contaminates a busy next turn.",
    "Admitted onMemoryRetrieved writes are fully awaited before terminal reflection/durability fence/ack; cancellation does not abandon a pending feedback write.",
    "Resume counters, fast retrieval, rejection, soft timeout and session races retain their contracts."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The runtime cannot prevent side effects inside a host callback that violates the documented read-only preparation contract. Production composition satisfies it.",
    "The in-flight slot is per runtime, shared across its workspaces; busy turns explicitly skip optional memory without cross-workspace content reuse.",
    "Real feedback writes remain fully awaited and may delay cancellation; they are not covered by the read-only abandonment boundary.",
